  "worked_solution": "Newton\u2019s second law states that\n\n$$\nF=ma,\n$$\n\nwhere $F$ is the *resultant* force, $m$ is the mass, and $a$ is the acceleration.\n\nTo compute the acceleration vector, we differentiate the velocity vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\u27e8\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}+2),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}\\,(6\\sqrt{t}+2\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t)\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e83{t}^{2},\\,\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{t}}+2\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t\u27e9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the resultant force $F$ at time $t$ equals\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F & =ma \\\\  & =2\\cdot \u27e83{t}^{2},\\,\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{t}}+2\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e86{t}^{2},\\,\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{t}}+4\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t\u27e9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhen $t=1\\,\\text{s},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(1) & =\u27e86(1)^{2},\\,\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{1}}+4\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(1)\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e86,\\,6+4\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(1)\u27e9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the magnitude of $F(1)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|F(1)| & =\\sqrt{(6)^{2}+{(6+4\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(1))}^{2}} \\\\  & \u224810,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer.\n\nSo, the magnitude of the resultant force is $10\\,\\text{N}.$",
